# Astro Rules — GoodEpoch Cursor Rules Pack v1
# Applies to: Astro 5.x
# Stack: Astro 5, TypeScript 5.5+, optional React/Svelte/Vue islands

## Mental Model: HTML-First, Islands for Interactivity

- Astro ships zero JavaScript by default. Every interactive piece must be explicitly opted in
- "Islands architecture": interactive components are hydrated independently
- Perfect for: content sites, docs, marketing, blogs, anything where most UI is static
- Use Astro for the shell/layout/content, UI framework (React/Svelte) only for interactive islands

## Component Types

- `.astro` components: server-rendered, no JavaScript in browser unless you add a `<script>`
- UI framework components (React, Svelte, Vue): hydrated with `client:*` directive
- Markdown/MDX: content collections for blog posts, docs, etc.

## Astro Component Syntax

```astro
---
// Component Script (runs on server at build/request time)
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content'
import PostCard from '../components/PostCard.astro'

const posts = await getCollection('blog')
const { title, description } = Astro.props
---

<!-- Template (pure HTML output, no virtual DOM) -->
<article>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p>{description}</p>
  {posts.map(post => <PostCard post={post} />)}
</article>

<style>
  /* Scoped CSS — no class name conflicts */
  article { max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
```

## Islands — Interactive Components

- Use `client:load` for components needed immediately on page load (rare)
- Use `client:idle` for components that can wait until browser is idle (navigation, search)
- Use `client:visible` for components below the fold (comments, charts)
- Use `client:media` for responsive breakpoint-specific components
- NEVER use `client:load` for everything — defeats the purpose of Astro:
  ```astro
  <!-- Bad: hydrates immediately, blocks -->
  <SearchBar client:load />
  
  <!-- Good: hydrates when visible in viewport -->
  <CommentSection client:visible />
  
  <!-- Good: hydrates when browser is idle -->
  <NavigationMenu client:idle />
  ```

## Content Collections (Astro 5)

- Define typed schemas with zod for all content:
  ```typescript
  // src/content/config.ts
  import { defineCollection, z } from 'astro:content'
  
  export const collections = {
    blog: defineCollection({
      type: 'content',
      schema: ({ image }) => z.object({
        title: z.string(),
        description: z.string(),
        pubDate: z.coerce.date(),
        hero: image().optional(),
        tags: z.array(z.string()).default([]),
        draft: z.boolean().default(false),
      })
    })
  }
  ```
- Query with `getCollection('blog', entry => !entry.data.draft)` to filter drafts
- Use `getEntry` for single entry lookup by slug

## Routing

- File-based routing under `src/pages/`
- `[slug].astro` for dynamic routes
- Static routes: export `getStaticPaths()` returning all possible params
- SSR routes: no `getStaticPaths` needed, runs on demand
- API routes: `src/pages/api/*.ts` that export GET/POST handlers

## Server Side Rendering (SSR)

- Enable SSR in `astro.config.mjs`: `output: 'server'` or `output: 'hybrid'`
- Hybrid mode: static by default, opt-in to SSR per page with `export const prerender = false`
- Access request cookies: `Astro.cookies.get('session')?.value`
- Redirect: `return Astro.redirect('/login')`
- Environment variables: `import.meta.env.SECRET` for server-only, `PUBLIC_*` prefix for client

## Image Optimization

- Always use `<Image>` from `astro:assets` — never raw `<img>` for local images
- Automatic format conversion (WebP/AVIF), lazy loading, sizing
- Remote images need `domains` or `remotePatterns` in config

## Performance Defaults

- Zero JavaScript ships unless you use `client:*` — keep it that way
- Inline critical CSS: Astro's scoped styles are inlined automatically
- Use `import.meta.glob` for bulk imports of content files
- Preload fonts with `<link rel="preload">` in BaseLayout

## Layouts

- Create `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro` with HTML boilerplate, meta tags, fonts
- Pass page-specific metadata via props: `<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc}>`
- Slot content with `<slot />` — named slots for header/footer overrides

## Integrations

- `@astrojs/react` for React islands
- `@astrojs/tailwind` for Tailwind CSS
- `@astrojs/sitemap` for automatic sitemap generation
- `@astrojs/mdx` for MDX support in content collections
- `@astrojs/vercel` or `@astrojs/cloudflare` for deployment
